{
  "title": "98: al-Bayyenah البينة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nلَمْ يَكُنِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ وَالْمُشْرِكِيْنَ مُنْفَكِّيْنَ حَتّٰى تَاْتِيَهُمُ الْبَيِّنَةُ ۙ‏(1)\nLAM YAKONIL LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN AHLIL KETAABE WAL-MUSHREKEENA MUN-FAKKEENA HATTA TAA-TEYAHOMUL BAYYENATO. \nThose who disbelieved from among the followers of the Book and the polytheists could not have separated (from the faithful) until there had come to them the clear evidence: \nرَسُوْلٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ يَتْلُوْا صُحُفًا مُّطَهَّرَةً ۙ‏(2)\nRASOOLUM MENAL LAAHE YATLOO SOHOFAM MOTAHHARATAN. \nAn apostle from Allah, reciting pure pages, \nفِيْهَا كُتُبٌ قَيِّمَةٌ ؕ‏(3)\nFEEHAA KOTOBUN QAYYEMAH. \nWherein are all the right ordinances. \nوَمَا تَفَرَّقَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّنَةُ ؕ‏(4)\nWA MAA TAFARRAQAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA ILLAA MIM BA’DE MAA JAA-AT-HOMUL BAYYENAH. \nAnd those who were given the Book did not become divided except after clear evidence had come to them. \nوَمَاۤ اُمِرُوْۤا اِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ ۙ حُنَفَآءَ وَيُقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُؤْتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ وَذٰلِكَ دِيْنُ الْقَيِّمَةِ ؕ‏(5)\nWA MAAA OMEROO ILLAA LE-YA’BODUL LAAHA MUKHLESEENA LAHUD DEENA, HONAFAAA-A WA YOQEEMUS SALAATA WA YOA-TUZ ZAKAATA WA ZAALEKA DEENUL QAYYEMAH. \nAnd they were not enjoined anything except that they should serve Allah, being sincere to Him in obedience, upright, and keep up prayer and pay the poor-rate, and that is the right religion. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ وَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ فِىْ نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمْ شَرُّ الْبَرِيَّةِ ؕ‏(6)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN AHLIL KETAABE WAL-MUSHREKEENA FEE NAARE JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, OO-LAAA-EKA HUM SHARRUL BARIYYAH. \nSurely those who disbelieve from among the followers of the Book and the polytheists shall be in the fire of hell, abiding therein; they are the worst of men. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمْ خَيْرُ الْبَرِيَّةِ ؕ‏(7)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE, OO-LAAA-EKA HUM KHAYRUL BARIYYAH. \n(As for) those who believe and do good, surely they are the -best of men. \nجَزَآؤُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ جَنّٰتُ عَدْنٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ رَضِىَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوْا عَنْهُ ؕ ذٰلِكَ لِمَنْ خَشِىَ رَبَّهٗ‏(8)\nJA-ZAAA-OHUM I’NDA RABBEHIM JANNAATO A’DNIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAA, RAZEYAL LAAHO A’NHUM WA RAZOO A’NH, ZAALEKA LEMAN KHASHEYA RABBAH.\nTheir reward with their Lord is gardens of perpetuity beneath which rivers flow, abiding therein for ever; Allah is well pleased with them and they are well pleased with Him; that is for him who fears his Lord. ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Bayyenah (The Clear Evidence)\nThis Surah has 8 verses and it is a ‘Madani’ Surah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that if people knew the benefits of reciting this Surah, they would leave their work in order to learn it.\nIf a person recites this Surah at night, then Allah (s.w.t.) sends angels to protect the reciter and his faith is also secure. The angels seek forgiveness for him. The reward for reciting this Surah is equal to all those things on this Earth upon which the sun shines.\nWriting and drinking water of this Surah is beneficial for cure of ailments. Surah al-Bayyinah is also good for pregnant women and helps to ensure their safety and the safety of their babies. Reciting this Surah before eating food removes any ill effects of the foods."
